"notes": "Modified cash basis village. Governmental data from the governmental funds statement (p4, Total column); beginning cash = fund balance 9/30/2024 564,450. Transfers in/out net to 0 in the Total column (General -32,499, Debt Service +32,499), so top-level transfers are null. Other financing = other grant 3,740 + gain on sale 4,002; loan proceeds 250,000 in debt_proceeds. Identity: 564,450 + 376,947 - 670,463 + 250,000 + 7,742 = 528,676. Business-type (proprietary fund): the proprietary receipts/disbursements statement (report p15) is not in the trimmed PDF, so receipts 190,042 (charges for services) and disbursements 162,615 come from the statement of activities (p2) as single totals; net position 13,698 beginning to 41,125 ending is cash (modified cash). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position, Total column (p1). Detail: General Fund revenue from the budget schedule (p5); General Fund expenditures from the departmental schedules (pp6-9), which supersede the function-only lines on p5 (not double counted); Debt Service fund from p10. On p4 the Street and Police labels are swapped relative to pp2, 7, 8; recorded per the schedules. Page layout of trimmed PDF: p1 net position, p2 activities, p3 balance sheet, p4 receipts/disbursements, p5 GF budget, p6-9 departments, p10 debt service, p11 proprietary net position (cash 41,125, no liabilities). Read pages 1-11 of 11"
